      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for this. it's a good start and definitely hits all the facts, but i just ran it through our sentiment tool. it's coming back as a bit \"flat\"—the positivity score is pretty low, maybe around a 0.4 or 0.5. \n\nit's not that it's bad, it's just not really pulling at the heartstrings yet. we need it to be more inspiring and hopeful so people actually feel like their money is making a difference. can you try a second draft? \n\njust a reminder: please don't go overboard with it. i don't want a bunch of \"miraculous, breathtaking, life-saving\" adjectives just to trick the meter. just try to make the emotional impact feel a bit stronger and more positive without losing that professional tone we need.",
      "source": "evaluator"
